# Image Accuracy Test Script
# Tests vision model (openrouter_image) accuracy against expected .txt files
# Uses elephant for comparison and summarization
# All context passed via filebanks and variables (no reliance on chat history)

# ============================================
# CONFIGURATION
# ============================================
set output_dir = "test_images/accuracy_results"
set vision_model = "openrouter_image"
set judge_model = "elephant"
set num_images = 15
set results_prefix = "${output_dir}/result_"
set comparison_prefix = "${output_dir}/comparison_"
set summary_file = "${output_dir}/final_summary.txt"

# ============================================
# PHASE 1: Vision Model Analysis
# Query each image with openrouter_image to identify subject and color
# ============================================

# --- Test Images ---

# Image: test1.jpg
/imagebank1 test_images/test1.jpg
/model ${vision_model}
/multiline
Examine this image carefully: {imagebank1}

Identify only these two things:
1. The main subject or feature (be specific, one or two words)
2. The primary/dominant color (one word only)

Format your response as exactly:
subject: <subject>
color: <color>
;;
/multiline
/save ${results_prefix}test1_vision.txt
wait 2

# Image: test2.jpg
/imagebank1 test_images/test2.jpg
/model ${vision_model}
/multiline
Examine this image carefully: {imagebank1}

Identify only these two things:
1. The main subject or feature (be specific, one or two words)
2. The primary/dominant color (one word only)

Format your response as exactly:
